        "original_id": "8f674c8e-0113-56b8-b528-331bbb49531f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Miles Kane, Carl Barât, Pete Doherty\n- Bands: The Libertines, The Last Shadow Puppets\n- Songs: \"Don't Forget Who You Are\"\n- Albums: Don't Forget Who You Are, Anthems for Doomed Youth\n- Places: London, United Kingdom\n\nFacts:\n- The Libertines are an English rock band formed in London in 1997 by frontmen Carl Barât and Pete Doherty.\n- Miles Peter Kane was born on 17 March 1986 and is an English musician.\n- Miles Kane is best known as a solo artist and as the co-frontman of The Last Shadow Puppets.\n- \"Don't Forget Who You Are\" is a song by Miles Kane from his second studio album Don't Forget Who You Are.\n- \"Don't Forget Who You Are\" was released as a digital download in the United Kingdom on 3 June 2013.\n- Anthems for Doomed Youth is the third studio album by the English garage rock band The Libertines.\n- Anthems for Doomed Youth was released on 11 September 2015.",
